Make the prefix-cache-hit-rate rolling window configurable via
VLLM_CACHE_METRICS_WINDOW (default 1000, unchanged from upstream's
hardcoded value -- there's even a "# TODO: Make the interval configurable."
comment already sitting on this line in vLLM 0.27.1).

Why: the periodic "prefix cache hit: NN%" log line (loggers.py) is a
sliding-window average over the *last N requests this engine has served*,
not a per-request number. With the default N=1000, on this single-user
box that window easily spans an entire day's mixed traffic (this
conversation's tests, deliberate cold-start benchmarks via
local_chat_test.py -p, title-generation calls, etc.), so the logged
percentage rarely reflects what's actually happening in the request you
just sent. Setting VLLM_CACHE_METRICS_WINDOW=1 (or a small number) makes
that log line track only the most recent request(s) instead.

Applies to all three CachingMetrics instances LoggingStatLogger creates
(prefix, connector/external-tier, and multimodal) so the window stays
consistent across every "X% ... external Y%, total Z%" figure on that
line.

--- a/v1/metrics/loggers.py
+++ b/v1/metrics/loggers.py
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
 
 import logging
+import os
 import time
 from abc import ABC, abstractmethod
 from collections import deque
@@ -142,10 +143,17 @@
         self.last_scheduler_stats = SchedulerStats()
 
         # Caching metrics. This cannot be reset.
-        # TODO: Make the interval configurable.
-        self.prefix_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics()
-        self.connector_prefix_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics()
-        self.mm_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics()
+        # request-logging: window made configurable via
+        # VLLM_CACHE_METRICS_WINDOW (default 1000, matching upstream's
+        # previous hardcoded value) -- with the default 1000-request
+        # rolling window, the periodic "prefix cache hit: NN%" log line
+        # blends in a lot of unrelated traffic (other sessions, one-off
+        # cold-start tests, etc.), so a small window lets it reflect only
+        # the last few requests instead.
+        _cache_metrics_window = int(os.environ.get("VLLM_CACHE_METRICS_WINDOW", "1000"))
+        self.prefix_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics(_cache_metrics_window)
+        self.connector_prefix_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics(_cache_metrics_window)
+        self.mm_caching_metrics = CachingMetrics(_cache_metrics_window)
 
         model_config = self.vllm_config.model_config
         is_diffusion = model_config is not None and model_config.is_diffusion
